{
  "id": "6pi3lt7",
  "title": "CHAPTER 1 : CALCULATION TECHNIQUES AND MATHEMATICAL BASICS",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "d4e1ygx",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Why Calculation Techniques Are the Real Foundation of RRB Maths</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Recommended Squares",
          "value": "1–30",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Rule",
          "value": "BODMAS",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Skill",
          "value": "Fraction-Percent",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Exam Focus",
          "value": "Speed & Accuracy",
          "icon": "clock"
        }
      ],
      "id": "zi694ou"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Always follow the BODMAS order of operations: Brackets → Orders → Division → Multiplication → Addition → Subtraction.",
        "Memorizing percentage-to-fraction equivalents and square values from 1 to 30 drastically cuts down calculation time.",
        "Approximation strategies should be deployed when options are widely spaced and speed is prioritized over exact precision.",
        "Developing shortcut techniques for fractions, decimals, ratios, and averages prevents common arithmetic mistakes under exam pressure."
      ],
      "id": "f2y9w7h"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "43jotc9",
      "content": "In competitive examinations, mathematics is not only about knowing concepts but also about executing calculations rapidly and accurately. A student who takes excessive time in basic arithmetic automatically falls behind, regardless of conceptual clarity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "52por7w",
      "content": "Calculation speed directly affects:"
    },
    {
      "id": "tyz85oq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Attempt rate</li><li>Accuracy</li><li>Confidence</li><li>Time available for difficult questions</li></ul>",
        "Attempt rate",
        "Accuracy",
        "Confidence",
        "Time available for difficult questions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ua4jhxu",
      "content": "Therefore, this chapter must be mastered before moving to advanced arithmetic topics."
    },
    {
      "id": "xdg2rwy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "The BODMAS Rule – Order of Operations"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "flyoi5g",
      "content": "Whenever an expression contains multiple operations, they must be solved in a specific order known as BODMAS:"
    },
    {
      "id": "50794r4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Brackets → Orders (powers/roots) → Division → Multiplication → Addition → Subtraction. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "772el29",
      "content": "48 ÷ 6 × 2 + 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wdrqtzn",
      "content": "Step 1: Division → 48 ÷ 6 = 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9pllj6q",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiplication → 8 × 2 = 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ugsjws0",
      "content": "Step 3: Addition → 16 + 5 = 21"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bpq60f8",
      "content": "Ignoring operation order is one of the most common mistakes in RRB exams."
    },
    {
      "id": "axm03va",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Fraction Mastery – The Backbone of Fast Arithmetic"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ko3e68s",
      "content": "Fractions appear in percentages, ratio, time-work, profit-loss, and algebra. Instant recognition is essential."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rv9yc56",
      "content": "Memorize the following conversions: 1/2 = 0.5 = 50%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5ota2u6",
      "content": "1/3 =0.333 = 33.33%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9h3c4br",
      "content": "2/3 = 0.666 = 66.67%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nt2mcxw",
      "content": "1/4 = 0.25 = 25%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "79e3gbm",
      "content": "3/4 = 0.75 = 75%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3fgtksk",
      "content": "1/5 = 0.2 = 20%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "610dm07",
      "content": "1/6 = 16.67%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k3fg051",
      "content": "1/8 = 0.125 = 12.5%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7ntfvux",
      "content": "1/9 = 11.11%"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jrywy3t",
      "content": "1/10 = 0.1 = 10%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zftvklj",
      "content": "Students who memorize these rarely need long calculations."
    },
    {
      "id": "u7yb7zh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Decimal Operations – Accuracy Matters"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fuh8r7l",
      "content": "While multiplying decimals, ignore the decimal temporarily, multiply normally, and then place the decimal based on total decimal places."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y4myefl",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "x5i2230",
      "content": "2.5 × 0.4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9empnop",
      "content": "25 × 4 = 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3h2fr4v",
      "content": "Total decimal places = 2 Answer = 1.00 = 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "etzzehc",
      "content": "Always double-check decimal placement."
    },
    {
      "id": "tw2r9e0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Percentage–Fraction Equivalents (Extremely Important)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "seevdpm",
      "content": "Many RRB problems become trivial when percentages are converted into fractions."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hiptm3l",
      "content": "5% = 1/20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "whh2x29",
      "content": "10% = 1/10"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zuajc48",
      "content": "12.5% = 1/8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dt26gps",
      "content": "20% = 1/5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fobyovc",
      "content": "25% = 1/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q628zdi",
      "content": "40% = 2/5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "it7x6ai",
      "content": "50% = 1/2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "e68bhnm",
      "content": "75% = 3/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oqpctv3",
      "content": "This skill dramatically increases solving speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "3usefn1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Squares You Must Memorize (1–30 Recommended)"
    },
    {
      "id": "41flyti",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "o0yzagn",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB COMPLETE MATHS/images/image_o0yzagn.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vmf5j0c",
      "content": "<img></img>Memorization of squares reduces calculation time in algebra, geometry, and simplification. Important ones:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "su52itb",
      "content": "11² = 121"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "286dmgk",
      "content": "12² = 144"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g8d3ipw",
      "content": "13² = 169"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "txx6cyn",
      "content": "14² = 196"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "08cwqx5",
      "content": "15² = 225"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8pbb5tx",
      "content": "16² = 256"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pkln6co",
      "content": "18² = 324"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7jgb4zu",
      "content": "20² = 400"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iuyeuqw",
      "content": "25² = 625"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ws3t2c2",
      "content": "30² = 900"
    },
    {
      "id": "aj6y3uc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Cube Values for Fast Recognition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6jrhqdx",
      "content": "Memorize cubes at least up to 20. 4³ = 64"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "db50f0v",
      "content": "5³ = 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4onrlk9",
      "content": "6³ = 216"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ktv3ojj",
      "content": "8³ = 512"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k9fq9n5",
      "content": "9³ = 729"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9naboth",
      "content": "10³ = 1000"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h76csyl",
      "content": "Cubes frequently appear in approximation questions."
    },
    {
      "id": "h0j8ec0",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Multiplication Speed Techniques </strong>Technique 1: Break numbers strategically. Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7q5p2pd",
      "content": "48 × 25"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w93f50o",
      "content": "= 48 × (100/4)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ljlmrxw",
      "content": "= 4800 ÷ 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w7r6ytk",
      "content": "= 1200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3jn5gi8",
      "content": "Technique 2: Use distributive property. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "aqilpxm",
      "content": "103 × 27"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "isvodll",
      "content": "= (100 × 27) + (3 × 27)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cel6pdq",
      "content": "= 2700 + 81"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8572r2u",
      "content": "= 2781"
    },
    {
      "id": "3mdlo5d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Division Shortcuts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k9tnqpc",
      "content": "Before dividing, reduce the expression. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xxgjjb3",
      "content": "720 ÷ 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1tgacxk",
      "content": "Divide both by 8:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jlq3gyc",
      "content": "90 ÷ 2 = 45."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdytas3",
      "content": "Factor cancellation saves time."
    },
    {
      "id": "8fk6tgf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Approximation Strategy – When Speed Matters More Than Precision"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e4v4xu9",
      "content": "Approximation is useful when answer choices are widely spaced."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Exact Calculation",
        "Approximation Strategy"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Primary Goal",
          "Absolute mathematical precision",
          "Rapid option elimination"
        ],
        [
          "Best Application",
          "Close option choices or simple values",
          "Data Interpretation and complex division"
        ],
        [
          "Time Required",
          "Higher time consumption",
          "Significantly reduced calculation time"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "bd0rk0a"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y8n84ke",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7t6v5e4",
      "content": "598 + 201 + 99 ≈ 600 + 200 + 100 = 900."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cyq4584",
      "content": "Use approximation carefully when exact answers are unnecessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "812h7d9",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>The Power of Multiplying by 5, 25,125 </strong>Multiply by 5 → multiply by 10 and divide by 2. Multiply by 25 → multiply by 100 and divide by 4."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "po80q7m",
      "content": "Multiply by 125 → multiply by 1000 and divide by 8."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "btdir6l",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "x3bp78r",
      "content": "64 × 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "r2f7fuk",
      "content": "= 64000 ÷ 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lhqtjn7",
      "content": "= 8000."
    },
    {
      "id": "ggkmtee",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Simplification Through Factorization </strong>Look for numbers that combine into powers of 10. Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mkppfe7",
      "content": "32 × 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "577ju6o",
      "content": "= 32 × (1000/8)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ncmrei9",
      "content": "= 4000."
    },
    {
      "id": "7p62ope",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio-Based Calculation Trick"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0igswp5",
      "content": "If A : B = 3 : 5 and total = 64, Sum of ratio parts = 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xbcphy7",
      "content": "Value of one part = 8 A = 24, B = 40."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t493aa9",
      "content": "Ratio logic speeds up arithmetic problems."
    },
    {
      "id": "nbupcal",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Average Shortcut"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tmwjo1p",
      "content": "Average = Sum / Number of observations. If five numbers average 20, their total is: 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l7uu4ku",
      "content": "× 20 = 100."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bencvg8",
      "content": "This shortcut is frequently used."
    },
    {
      "id": "ql4nyjk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Common Calculation Mistakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ybg9ihs",
      "content": "Students often lose marks because they:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kr37t8y",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Ignore BODMAS",
        "Misplace decimals",
        "Forget fraction conversions",
        "Rush calculations",
        "Avoid approximation when useful Speed must never compromise accuracy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qp992f9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Speed Development Framework"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mjcvhua",
      "content": "To build calculation speed:"
    },
    {
      "id": "zirhdpg",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Memorize tables upto 25.",
        "Learn squares up to 30.",
        "Practice daily mental maths.",
        "Avoid unnecessary written steps.",
        "Consistency creates automaticity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4st2hvv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Exam-Level Practice Questions with Solutions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hgul4u5",
      "content": "Question 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qfr1z8l",
      "content": "Evaluate: 24 + 36 ÷ 6 × 3. Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8l8j0nh",
      "content": "36 ÷ 6 = 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wicrf4n",
      "content": "6 × 3 = 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wplcylp",
      "content": "24 + 18 = 42."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "67l8ge9",
      "content": "Final Answer: 42"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jufokgm",
      "content": "Question 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ypnlxc6",
      "content": "Find the value of 48 × 25. 25 = 100/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "BODMAS priority missteps are a major source of negative marking in simplification problems.",
        "Converting complex percentage values into simplified fractions is frequently tested in Data Interpretation sets.",
        "Decimal placement errors during division shortcuts are common traps designed by examiners."
      ],
      "id": "24idfym"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ah2het1",
      "content": "48 × 100 = 4800"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r0fkxhe",
      "content": "4800 ÷ 4 = 1200."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "70ezidu",
      "content": "Final Answer: 1200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b5qmzeq",
      "content": "Question 3:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qmwr7vo",
      "content": "Convert 12.5% into a fraction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ix1cw0",
      "content": "12.5/100 = 125/1000 = 1/8."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wpoqr79",
      "content": "Final Answer: 1/8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "96ovvx7",
      "content": "Question 4:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wtk0yqg",
      "content": "Find the average of 10, 20, 30, 40."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yissb3n",
      "content": "Sum = 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hz1uvcj",
      "content": "Average = 100 ÷ 4 = 25."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g9auhah",
      "content": "Final Answer: 25"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gki90xw",
      "content": "Question 5:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "941tkqg",
      "content": "Evaluate: 2.5 × 0.2."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "t2ln8rf",
      "content": "25 × 2 = 50"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u4kitdc",
      "content": "Two decimal places → 0.50 = 0.5. Final Answer: 0.5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sn537ot",
      "content": "Question 6:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2krzmlm",
      "content": "Approximate 497 + 304."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pmqgob9",
      "content": "=&gt;500 + 300 = 800."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bim4g20",
      "content": "Final Answer: Approximately 800."
    },
    {
      "id": "46flacu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Final Insight"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1f09m3l",
      "content": "Calculation is not a preliminary skill; it is the engine that drives success in quantitative aptitude. Master calculation techniques to experience a dramatic improvement in speed, confidence, and accuracy across every mathematical chapter."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}